 suit reveal which felt tacked on  and totally didn't fit the rest of the  movie in fact that moment in the final  film felt more like a Marvel post-credit  scene for an Iron Man movie because the  way the tech wrapped itself around the  scientists body screamed Tony Stark's  nanotech suit to me also I wonder why  the studio didn't think of simply  replacing Schwarzenegger as cameo with  say Danny Glover from predator 2 Black's  original script also reveals another  deleted section from the last act in the  film that we never got to see in the  original story there was a group of  friends  predators hidden away in area 52 we've  been working with the secret government  organization to help defend the earth  against the incoming wave of upgrade  predators in fact they were actually  going to fight alongside McKenna's team  and you can see these friendly predators  decked out in military camouflage  uniform and on set photos trailers also  show footage from those tank scenes  which never made it into the final movie  and in the original script the Upgrade  predator had also been tasked with  tracking down and killing those friendly  predators tied in with the original  story about predators working with the  government was edward james olmos as  character who ended up getting chopped  out of the movie almost played a  four-star general over sterling kate  brown's character and it seems like he  was going to be the real big villain of  the movie according to Shane black  almost his character was trying to  recruit the first predator that arrived  on earth and it communicated with him  the actor was due to appear in two  scenes but they were both deleted when  black decided he had one bad guy too  many in the story and so sterling K  Brown took over as a chief human  antagonist by the way one of the movies  almost as well known for is Blade Runner  where his character is known for making  little origami unicorns so wonder if  Black included that little tinfoil  unicorn 